1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:01,567
Seven a.m.

2
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:02,600
Two people,

3
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,600
two districts apart.

4
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,333
In Punjab,

5
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,400
a pellet maker has

6
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,100
a warehouse full of stock,

7
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,833
and no one to sell to.

8
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:09,633
In Haryana,

9
00:00:09,633 --> 00:00:10,300
a factory manager

10
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,667
needs fuel by Friday,

11
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:13,767
and no one to buy from.

12
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,400
She calls three traders.

13
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,333
He checks old WhatsApp groups.

14
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:19,300
She hears three different prices.

15
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:20,867
He gets no reply.

16
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,900
By evening,

17
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:23,733
his boiler runs short.

18
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,300
Her stock is still waiting.

19
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:27,633
They just never found each other.

20
00:00:27,633 --> 00:00:27,833
That is the real

21
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:29,767
gap in India's biomass trade.

22
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:30,567
Not supply.

23
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:31,400
Not demand.

24
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,500
The connection.

25
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:35,300
IndiaBiomass is building it.
